Make Me a Hanzi
---------------
https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi

Source of every stroke outline and stroke median in `public/data/char/*.json`,
and of the pinyin readings, English definitions, radicals and decompositions in
`public/data/index.json`.

Make Me a Hanzi is released under the LGPL, and its glyph data derives from the
Arphic PL fonts, which are distributed under the ARPHIC PUBLIC LICENSE. Its
definitions come from CC-CEDICT (CC BY-SA 4.0) and the Unicode Consortium's
Unihan database.

Per the ARPHIC PUBLIC LICENSE, the character graphics may be freely copied and
redistributed provided this notice is retained and derivative font software
carries the same licence.


hanzi-writer-data
-----------------
https://github.com/chanind/hanzi-writer-data

Stroke data for characters not vendored in this repository is fetched at runtime
from the jsDelivr mirror of this package. It is itself derived from Make Me a
Hanzi and carries the same LGPL / ARPHIC terms.


complete-hsk-vocabulary
-----------------------
https://github.com/drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary

Source of the HSK 3.0 band and corpus frequency used to rank characters and to
populate the HSK section, and — by way of the course files described below — of
the vocabulary, pinyin and meanings in `public/data/hsk/level-*.json`. MIT
licensed. Its meanings derive from CC-CEDICT (CC BY-SA 4.0).


mssl-strok
----------
https://github.com/soleysok/mssl-strok

Source of the HSK course *arrangement* in `public/data/hsk/level-*.json`: which
words each unit teaches, in what order, under what title. `scripts/build-hsk-
data.py` copies that repository's own committed course files and trims them to
the fields this app renders, rather than deriving a second, slightly different
course from the vocabulary list. Same authors, MIT licensed, and the words
themselves carry the complete-hsk-vocabulary and CC-CEDICT terms above.
